From u9d7c257e609d0807 at groups.google.com  Thu Jul  2 14:44:49 2015
From: u9d7c257e609d0807 at groups.google.com (amit gal)
Date: Thu, 02 Jul 2015 14:44:49 +0000
Subject: Re: [Israel RUG] How to anonymizing id field?
Message-ID: <tWHE7YoN3XM.1vhC48MNqogJ@israel-r-user-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <tWHE7YoN3XM.FwUbgMDb61YJ@israel-r-user-group.groups.google.com>
References: <tWHE7YoN3XM.FwUbgMDb61YJ@israel-r-user-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/israel-r-user-group/c/tWHE7YoN3XM/m/1vhC48MNqogJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

1. Create a vector of unique ids across all your data.
2. Create a vector of new, anonimized, ids of the same length
3. Name the vector from step 2 using the vector in step 1
4. Anonimize your data
X$nid = all.anonimized[x$id]

